posting _IS NOT EMAIL_? It doesn't matter spit that
Google also runs an email facility, Usenet _IS NOT
IT_. How do you manage to stay this confused despite
manifold screams of protest from legions of long
time Usenet users?

That means:

   You don't call a posting "email" in prompt or
   informative messages.

   You don't quote "from " or "From " at the
   beginning of a line in a Usenet posting, either
   when transmitting it or when displaying it.

   You don't start the user off with a blank line or
   (now) two at the top of a followup reply into
